CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^\[loop_fn\.loop_invariant_step\.\d+\] line \d+ Check invariant after step for loop loop_fn\.0: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^Invariant check failed
--
Loop assigns inference inlines the callees of loop_fn before loop_fn's calls
are instrumented. When printf has already been instrumented, the arguments of
the call do not match its parameters any more, which made the inliner fail an
invariant on the argument of type unsigned short.
